00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:12.649
Just to kind of give you an example

325
00:16:12.649 --> 00:16:15.090
of what's being seen, the image on the left

326
00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:16.269
is basically, like I said,

327
00:16:16.269 --> 00:16:19.110
a composite of all the incoming video signals

328
00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:22.029
from all the render boxes that are being driven

329
00:16:22.029 --> 00:16:24.429
by NDisplay and Unreal Engine.

330
00:16:24.429 --> 00:16:26.909
Very helpful, very informative,

331
00:16:26.909 --> 00:16:29.090
and really gives your directors

332
00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:33.519
and virtual production supervisors some extra help.

333
00:16:33.519 --> 00:16:37.720
All right, now we also have LED wall technology

334
00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.879
and processors that we need to discuss.

335
00:16:39.879 --> 00:16:44.559
We have the Brompton processors and megapixel processors

336
00:16:44.559 --> 00:16:47.399
that are commonly used at the stages that we have.

