00:16:47.399 --> 00:16:52.080
In this example, I'm showing you the Brompton Tessera SX40.

338
00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:54.000
That's what's driving the particular wall

339
00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.240
here at the latte stage.

340
00:16:56.240 --> 00:17:01.240
This basically converts 4K video into 10 gig IP video.

341
00:17:02.039 --> 00:17:06.960
Now, this IP video then travels over fiber optic wire

342
00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:10.839
to your distribution nodes,

343
00:17:10.839 --> 00:17:13.119
which typically are located behind the wall.

344
00:17:13.119 --> 00:17:15.440
And we're gonna look at all that here on the stage

